{
  "_doc": "SCOUT-1 (Rowan, 2026-11-12): the growth product manager looks for the state of the art and files what it finds. foundation/scout.py reads each source on a weekly clock, scores every new entry against the gap register in doctrine/market.json and the needs below, files a growth queue item (Q-SCOUT-*) for each entry over the threshold, and re-weights its own sources from what was adopted. Sources are data: a pass that finds a better one adds it by PR; a source with `standard` is the release feed of a standard adopted in seed/standards/standards.json, and every new entry on it is filed as an item (STANDARDS-FIRST-1) (the scout also files a growth item when a source returns nothing for four passes). Read by foundation/scout.py, scripts and .github/workflows/scout.yml.",
  "threshold": 2.0,
  "max_per_run": 5,
  "window_days": 30,
  "weight": {"initial": 1.0, "floor": 0.25, "ceiling": 2.0, "decay": 0.8, "boost": 1.25, "quiet_passes": 4},
